# 06 §9 — adaptation
# RULE: power goes out at 3:00 every night, 11 minutes. Refrain: "Lights out, eyes in."
# COPING: 3 curtains per window (Pike's sells 900/yr) · bakery opens 3:11 · mayor's NOT LOOKING masks (wears 2)
# HERO: me, 10, now closes Bea's curtains (twice, like Dad). LOVED ONE: Bea, 6, leaves a cookie "for the one who turns the lights off".
# TABOO: looking outside. SEEDS: cookie gone (window locked) · fur high on the pole · 23 footprints, one per house ·
#        1994 newspaper "9 gone, all lights on" · it taps each window once per person (counting).
# ESCALATION: note "You looked." → lights out at 2:59 → knock on the roof → Bea turns her flashlight on.
# TWIST: "The giant was never hunting us. It was hiding us." That's why: lights out / checks windows / counts / cookies.
# PAYOFF: it takes Bea's cookie with 2 fingers, new note. STING (callback to the counting): 5 taps, "There are only 4 of us."
title: The 3AM Neighbor
id: the-3am-neighbor
lang: en
voice: narrator_c2

cast:
me    kid spiky #f2d232 | stripes_h #e7c43f #151515 | pants #151515
bea   kid ponytail #6b3f22 | pajamas_stars #7fb2ee #ffffff | bow
mom   adult bun #2a1d17 | cardigan #f0a6b8 #fff3f6 | pants #3b4a6b
dad   adult short #4a3426 | plaid #3a6ea5 #1d2b45 | pants #555555 | glasses
mayor adult short #2a2a2a | suit #1f2f5c #ffffff | pants #1f2f5c | tie mayor_chain mustache
beast creature furry_giant
eyes  creature shadow_eyes

== card night
In this town, the power goes out | card:clock text=3:00 title=AM push
== suburban_street night
at 3:00 every night. | est push
For exactly 11 minutes. | aer drift
== house_front night
Nobody looks outside. | est push
== bedroom night
Lights out, eyes in. | cu me:neutral push
That's the rule. | med me:shrug
== bedroom day
Every window in town has 3 curtains. | ins >window push
== card day
Mr. Pike's hardware store | card:sign_metal title="PIKE'S HARDWARE" text="CURTAINS 3 FOR $20"
== city_street day
sells 900 of them a year. | med extra:carry:smile@sidewalk
== card day
The bakery opens at 3:11. | card:sign_wood title="BAKERY" text="OPEN 3:11 AM" push
== town_square day
Never 3:00. | med extra2:shrug
Our mayor gave every family | med mayor:talk@plaque
a sleep mask that says | cu mayor:smirk push
NOT LOOKING. | med mayor:sign=NOT_LOOKING:grin push
He wears 2. | cu mayor:wink push
== town_square dusk
Every night, the whole town says it. | est crowd:16:talk>statue
"Lights out, eyes in." | med extra:talk q:town
== kitchen night
Like goodnight. | two mom:smile dad:smile
== bedroom night
My little sister Bea is 6. | med bea:wave:grin
And she's not scared of anything. | cu bea:smirk push
Every night, she leaves a cookie | mcu bea:reach:smile>window
on her windowsill. | ots bea:reach >window
"For the one who turns the lights off." | cu bea:talk:happy q:bea push
== living_room night
Dad checks all 7 curtains twice. | med dad:look_down>window
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7. | ots dad >window
== kitchen night
Mom hums the same song for 11 minutes. | mcu mom:sit:smile@seat1
In the dark. | wide mom:sit:smile@seat1 bea:sit:sleep@seat2
== bedroom night
And this year, I'm 10. | med me:grin
So I close Bea's curtains now. | two me:reach:smile bea:smile
Twice. Like Dad. | cu me:smirk push
== bedroom day
Then I started noticing things. | cu me:worried push
Every morning, Bea's cookie was gone. | ins >window push
== kitchen day
Mom said birds. | med mom:shrug
== bedroom day
The window was locked. | cu me:worried push
== suburban_street day
There was black fur on the power pole. | low s:poi:pole tiltu
Way up. Higher than our roof. | med me:point>pole
In the mud, there were footprints | wide >road push
as long as Dad's car. | med dad:surprised@driveway>road
One in front of every house. | aer panr
== card day
23 houses. 23 footprints. | card:notebook title="MY NOTES" text="23 houses. 23 footprints." push
== classroom day
At the library, I found a newspaper from 1994. | med me:look_down:book
== card day
9 people gone in one winter. | card:newspaper title="ELM DAILY - 1994" text="9 GONE IN ONE WINTER"
All from houses with the lights on. | card:newspaper title="ELM DAILY - 1994" text="All 9 houses had their lights on." push
== road_night night
The blackouts started the next year. | est drift
== bedroom night
Bea asked me who turns the lights off. | two bea:talk me:neutral
I said nobody. | med me:shrug
She said, "Then who eats the cookies?" | cu bea:talk:smirk q:bea push
So that night, at 3:00, | cu me:wide_eyes push
I opened my curtain. 1 inch. | ots me:reach >window
== suburban_street night
Something was walking down our street. | est beast:walk@road pov:vignette
== rooftops_sky night
Taller than the power poles. | low beast:walk@giant push
Black fur. | cu beast:loom push
A grin as wide as a car. | xcu beast push
== suburban_street night
It stopped at the Millers' house, | wide beast:lean@road
== rooftops_sky night
leaned down, and tapped their window. | cu beast:reach push
== house_front night
Tap. Tap. Tap. | ins >window shake
== living_room night
3 Millers. | med extra:scared extra2:scared extra3:scared
== bedroom night
Then the mayor's house. Tap. | med mayor:lie:sleep@bed
He lives alone. With his masks. | cu mayor:sleep push
== rooftops_sky night
Then it stopped at our house. | low beast:lean@giant push
== bedroom night
Tap. Tap. Tap. Tap. | ins >window shake
4. | cu me:wide_eyes push
== living_room night
Mom, Dad, Bea, me. | med mom:scared dad:scared bea:sleep
